# The round trip (axiom_auth_sign's aarch64 half;
# verus/isla/seams.md): `pacda x0, x1` then
# `autda x0, x1`, the canonical forms of sign and auth (pac-det.job.in
# shows every site computes the same function), in one configuration
# (pac-footprint.job.in), from a pointer below the configuration's VA
# limit 2^@VA@. Authenticating what signing returned, with the same
# modifier and key, gives the pointer back, whether or not EnDA is set.
# ComputePAC is uninterpreted: both instructions apply it to the same
# arguments, so its definition (QARMA or an implementation's own) does
# not matter. In the Armv9.4-A configurations (FEAT_PAuth2, FEAT_FPAC)
# run.sh adds `pc-step`, and `autda` is still `fallthrough`: its FPAC
# fault is one of the paths this job shows infeasible.
abstract ComputePAC
writes R0
no-mem-write
mem-reads 0
flags-preserved
assume (= ((_ extract 63 @VA@) init.R0) @ZEROS@)
assert (= final.R0 init.R0)
assert (= final._PC (bvadd init._PC #x0000000000000008))
